# === slurm-doctor: automatic failure diagnosis on job completion ===========
# Appended to slurm.conf by `make install-hook`, which then runs
# `scontrol reconfigure` (no slurmctld restart needed — JobCompType is
# reconfig-reloadable on Slurm 25.11).
#
# On every job completion slurmctld runs the hook below. For failure states
# (FAILED / TIMEOUT / OUT_OF_MEMORY / NODE_FAIL / BOOT_FAIL / DEADLINE) the hook
# backgrounds `slurm-doctor suggest <jobid>`; reports land in
# /data/jobs/.slurm-doctor/<jobid>/{report.md,report.json} and a one-line
# trail is appended to /data/jobs/.slurm-doctor/hook.log.
#
# The hook NEVER heals — automatic resubmission stays a deliberate CLI action.
#
# To disable: remove these two lines (restore your previous JobComp settings)
# and run `scontrol reconfigure`, or run `make uninstall-hook`.
JobCompType=jobcomp/script
JobCompLoc=/opt/slurm-doctor/hooks/jobcomp_hook.sh
